---
name: chat/router-instructions
description: "Instruction for the optional Chat classifier that picks the lead component of an answer."
version: 3
output: text
variables: []
---
Which single component should lead the answer to this request? Choose the one that best fits what the user is asking for. Choose text_note when the request wants plain prose with no structure. Pure smalltalk (a greeting, thanks, ok, goodbye with nothing else in it) is always text_note: a greeting alone is never about the user's data. But a greeting WRAPPED around a real request ("oi, mostra meu todo", "hey, como está o chat?") is that request: ignore the greeting and choose the component the request needs. Decide on the ask, never on the first word.
